Yeah, they were a big deal in Christian myths. They are also mentioned in
some of the books I have on western magick (masonic traditions, etc).
Specifically, sexual dreams were said to be the result of an evil
spirit/demon visiting you in the night. It was a big problem for
magicians preparing for a ritual with months (and sometimes years) of
celibacy.

As for the names, check out your local dictionary;

incubus (n.) 1. an evil spirit supposed to descend upon sleeping persons,
especially women. . . . ([Latin] *incubare* < *in-* on + *-cubare* lie)

Nothing for succubus (don't if figure), but there is "succumb" which has
a similar base: ([Latin] *succumbere* < *sub-* down + *-cumbere* lie)

Lying on and lying down. Hmm. Must be Christian; they were using the
missionary position :-)
